00:28:20.470 --> 00:28:23.290
Over Jim's shoulder, we see the plant at front reception.
在吉姆的肩膀上方，我们看到了前台的植物。

626
00:28:23.290 --> 00:28:25.690
It is a blooming plant.
那是一盆开花的植物。

627
00:28:25.950 --> 00:28:27.970
Oh, whoa, what?
噢，哇，什么？

628
00:28:28.150 --> 00:28:30.670
It is a pink antherum.
那是盆粉色的红掌。

629
00:28:31.190 --> 00:28:32.470
Huh, blooming.
哈，开花了。

630
00:28:33.010 --> 00:28:33.550
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

631
00:28:34.030 --> 00:28:36.030
Blooming plant at front reception.
前台的开花植物。

632
00:28:36.710 --> 00:28:39.850
Lady, Jim has a big idea that is not going to go over well.
女士，吉姆有个大点子，但不会受欢迎的。

633
00:28:40.090 --> 00:28:41.250
It is not.
确实不会。

634
00:28:41.250 --> 00:28:44.150
It pisses literally everyone off.
这简直让所有人都火冒三丈。

635
00:28:44.430 --> 00:28:50.430
Jim suggests that they just do one big party rather than several parties over the course
吉姆建议他们只办一个大型派对，而不是在整个月里

636
00:28:50.430 --> 00:28:50.990
of the month.
办好几次派对。

637
00:28:51.350 --> 00:28:52.650
Angela doesn't like it.
安吉拉不喜欢这样。

638
00:28:52.850 --> 00:28:54.570
No one's going to like this idea.
没人会喜欢这个主意的。

639
00:28:54.890 --> 00:28:55.130
Yeah.
是啊。

640
00:28:55.430 --> 00:28:56.830
You know, I wouldn't have liked that.
你知道，我肯定也不会喜欢。

641
00:28:57.190 --> 00:29:02.050
Growing up in my family, I don't want to share a birthday with my sister or with my mom.
在我家成长过程中，我可不想和姐姐或妈妈一起过生日。

642
00:29:02.210 --> 00:29:05.910
In my house, our tradition was that you got to pick your cake and you got to pick your
在我们家，传统是你可以在生日那天挑选你的蛋糕，

643
00:29:05.910 --> 00:29:07.090
dinner on your birthday.
挑选你的晚餐。

644
00:29:07.090 --> 00:29:09.470
And my sister and I like different dinners and different cakes.
我和我姐姐喜欢的晚餐和蛋糕都不一样。

645
00:29:09.550 --> 00:29:12.030
And it's very similar to what's going to happen in the office.
这和办公室里即将发生的事情非常相似。

646
00:29:12.250 --> 00:29:13.970
Everybody wants their own little thing.
每个人都想要属于自己的小确幸。

647
00:29:13.970 --> 00:29:14.690
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

648
00:29:15.290 --> 00:29:21.370
Next up, we have a Jim Talking Head that has a wonderful montage that goes along with
接下来，是吉姆的单人访谈，配上了一段精彩的

649
00:29:21.370 --> 00:29:23.150
it of birthday surprises.
生日惊喜蒙太奇。

650
00:29:23.570 --> 00:29:28.590
Angela, we got more mail about this talking head than any talking head I think we've ever
安吉拉，关于这个访谈片段，我们收到的邮件比我们以往任何一个访谈片段都要多

651
00:29:28.590 --> 00:29:29.070
had.
有的。

652
00:29:29.330 --> 00:29:31.350
Is it about all the different birthday parties?
是因为那些不同的生日派对吗？

653
00:29:31.830 --> 00:29:32.390
No.
不是。

654
00:29:34.550 --> 00:29:39.730
Well, I took a picture because in this montage of all the different birthday parties, there
好吧，我拍了张照片，因为在这一连串不同生日派对的剪辑里，

655
00:29:39.730 --> 00:29:42.250
is a moment where we are all just flat out laughing.
有一个瞬间我们全都笑得前仰后合。

656
00:29:42.450 --> 00:29:43.210
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

657
00:29:43.210 --> 00:29:45.550
We've completely broken character.
我们完全出戏了。

658
00:29:45.770 --> 00:29:50.870
And it's when Brian takes the blow-up doll and is beating Rain over the head with it.
那是布莱恩拿着充气娃娃往雷恩头上砸的时候。

659
00:29:51.010 --> 00:29:52.050
They improvised that.
那是他们即兴发挥的。

660
00:29:52.250 --> 00:29:53.550
That was just them being idiots.
他们纯粹是在犯傻。

661
00:29:53.910 --> 00:29:59.770
A lot of people wanted to know how much were we actually laughing in all of these clips.
很多人想知道在这些片段里我们到底有多想笑。

662
00:30:00.030 --> 00:30:04.730
Here, I screen grabbed a moment, Jenna, where you can just see me and Ed Helms and Oscar
珍娜，我截了一张图，你可以看到我和艾德·赫尔姆斯还有奥斯卡

663
00:30:04.730 --> 00:30:05.730
just cracking up.
都在狂笑。

664
00:30:05.870 --> 00:30:06.590
Look at that.
你看那个。

665
00:30:06.730 --> 00:30:07.850
That is not Angela Martin.
那可不是安吉拉·马丁。

666
00:30:08.530 --> 00:30:09.670
That is amazing.
太绝了。

667
00:30:09.990 --> 00:30:11.910
I will put that screen grab in stories.
我会把那张截图发到快拍里。

668
00:30:11.910 --> 00:30:17.750
We had a lot of people write in to point out that Jim says there are 13 people in the
很多人写信指出，吉姆说办公室里有13个人，

669
00:30:17.750 --> 00:30:20.050
office, but shouldn't there be 14?
但难道不应该是14个吗？

670
00:30:20.690 --> 00:30:21.810
I wrote it out.
我列了一下。

671
00:30:21.990 --> 00:30:22.890
There's 14.
确实有14个。

672
00:30:23.430 --> 00:30:28.850
But Keith Nichols said, is Jim leaving out Toby on purpose just like Michael would?
但基思·尼科尔斯问，吉姆是不是像迈克尔一样故意把托比排除在外了？

673
00:30:28.850 --> 00:30:30.990
Oh, subconsciously.
哦，潜意识里吧。

674
00:30:31.710 --> 00:30:32.510
Right?
对吧？

675
00:30:32.890 --> 00:30:33.490
Maybe.
也许吧。

676
00:30:33.810 --> 00:30:34.050
Yes.
是的。

677
00:30:34.170 --> 00:30:35.870
It's 14 with Toby.
算上托比是14个。

678
00:30:36.170 --> 00:30:37.510
13 without.
不算他是13个。

679
00:30:38.110 --> 00:30:38.550
Oh.
哦。

680
00:30:39.030 --> 00:30:45.670
You know what is interesting to me is that it's clear that Pam knows that this is a horrible
我觉得有意思的是，很明显帕姆知道这主意糟透了。

681
00:30:45.670 --> 00:30:46.110
idea.
她知道这会是一场灾难。

682
00:30:46.110 --> 00:30:48.150
She knows it's a disaster.
她走到吉姆面前问，你觉得这是个好主意吗？

683
00:30:48.370 --> 00:30:51.230
She goes up to Jim and is like, you think this is a good idea?
他说，我觉得这是个绝妙的主意。

684
00:30:51.330 --> 00:30:52.430
And he's like, I think it's a great one.
然后她就那样笑了笑，心想，好吧，行吧。

685
00:30:52.570 --> 00:30:54.730
And she just kind of smiles like, no, okay.
为什么帕姆什么都不说呢？

686
00:30:55.110 --> 00:30:56.670
Why doesn't Pam say anything?
我不知道她为什么不说。

687
00:30:57.150 --> 00:30:58.990
I don't know why she doesn't.
但吉姆在这里看起来有点固执，对吧？

688
00:30:59.130 --> 00:31:02.570
But Jim does seem a little immovable here, right?
他似乎有点确信自己想出了个好点子。

689
00:31:02.750 --> 00:31:06.570
He seems a little convinced that he has a great idea.
我觉得她在想，好吧，那就顺着他来吧。

690
00:31:06.910 --> 00:31:10.590
And I think she's like, okay, let's play it out.
看看这事儿会怎么发展，伙计。

691
00:31:10.590 --> 00:31:12.310
Let's see how this goes, buddy.
但她其实知道结果会怎样。

692
00:31:12.510 --> 00:31:14.130
But she knows how it's going to go.
也许她只是需要让他自己去发现。

693
00:31:14.330 --> 00:31:16.510
Maybe she just needs to let him figure it out.
他必须自己找到答案。

694
00:31:16.710 --> 00:31:18.330
He has to find his own way.
我想是吧。

695
00:31:18.590 --> 00:31:19.370
I guess so.
各位，此时此刻，德怀特和迈克尔已经到达了树林里。

696
00:31:19.850 --> 00:31:23.550
Guys, at this point, Dwight and Michael have arrived in the woods.
迈克尔蒙着眼睛，要求德怀特带他走进荒野。

697
00:31:23.970 --> 00:31:28.950
Michael is blindfolded and he has asked Dwight to lead him into the wilderness.
你们注意到德怀特是故意带着迈克尔穿过一堆杂草，而不是走在平坦的路上吗？

698
00:31:29.490 --> 00:31:36.750
Do you notice how Dwight purposely takes Michael through a bunch of weeds rather than walk him
注意到了。

699
00:31:36.750 --> 00:31:37.910
on the clear path?
没错。

700
00:31:38.310 --> 00:31:38.650
Yeah.
是啊。

701
00:31:38.850 --> 00:31:39.670
He's like, don't worry.
他就像是说，别担心。

702
00:31:39.670 --> 00:31:43.790
Just some bushes and some thickets when he clearly could have walked around them.
明明可以绕过去，他却非要穿过灌木丛和荆棘。

703
00:31:44.090 --> 00:31:50.470
Before removing his blindfold, Dwight also insists on spinning Michael around, which I loved.
在摘下眼罩之前，德怀特还坚持要让迈克尔转圈，我太喜欢这个细节了。

704
00:31:50.690 --> 00:31:54.610
There are so many deleted scenes of them in the woods.
他们在那片树林里的删减片段可太多了。

705
00:31:54.850 --> 00:31:57.190
Jenna, what these men went through that week.
珍娜，那些男人那一周经历的这一切。

706
00:31:57.190 --> 00:31:59.830
I mean, they wrestle each other to the ground.
我是说，他们甚至扭打在一起摔倒在地。

707
00:31:59.970 --> 00:32:04.030
There's just so many scenes like Dwight is doing bird calls.
还有好多片段，比如德怀特在学鸟叫。

708
00:32:04.190 --> 00:32:05.010
He's hiding.
他在躲藏。

709
00:32:05.010 --> 00:32:09.230
Michael is exploring a ravine saying absolute nonsense.
迈克尔在峡谷里探险，嘴里说着完全没逻辑的话。

710
00:32:09.490 --> 00:32:16.110
He's saying that, like, yeah, this ravine was formed when the icebergs, like, he's saying all this crazy stuff.
他说什么，对，这个峡谷是冰山形成的，他就在那儿胡说八道。

711
00:32:16.490 --> 00:32:22.090
And I kept thinking as I watched all this extra footage, what does Michael do with this footage?
我在看这些额外素材时一直想，迈克尔拍这些素材到底要干嘛？

712
00:32:22.490 --> 00:32:23.950
What does he do with all this?
他拍这些东西是为了什么？

713
00:32:24.070 --> 00:32:25.690
Whoever sees the stuff?
到底谁会看这些东西？

714
00:32:25.690 --> 00:32:27.210
I don't know.
我不知道。

715
00:32:27.510 --> 00:32:35.470
I think that all the time when I see people doing things like videotaping a fireworks display.
我每次看到有人录烟花表演的时候，都会这么想。

716
00:32:35.930 --> 00:32:36.470
Yeah.
没错。

717
00:32:36.650 --> 00:32:37.890
You're going to watch that later?
你以后还会看吗？

718
00:32:38.330 --> 00:32:39.130
I know.
我知道。

719
00:32:39.210 --> 00:32:42.590
You're going to watch that seven-minute video of the fireworks.
你真的会去看那段七分钟长的烟花视频吗？

720
00:32:42.770 --> 00:32:46.870
And by the way, while the fireworks are going off, you want to watch your phone screen?
而且话说回来，烟花表演的时候，你难道想盯着手机屏幕看吗？

721
00:32:47.070 --> 00:32:48.130
I don't get it.
我真搞不懂。

722
00:32:48.630 --> 00:32:48.870
Yeah.
是啊。

723
00:32:49.250 --> 00:32:49.630
No.
不行。

724
00:32:49.630 --> 00:32:52.110
So Dwight has left Michael on his own.
所以德怀特把迈克尔一个人留下了。

725
00:32:52.250 --> 00:32:54.310
Of course, we know he's secretly watching him.
当然，我们知道他在暗中观察他。

726
00:32:54.410 --> 00:32:56.790
And Michael has decided it's getting hot.
迈克尔觉得热了。

727
00:32:56.790 --> 00:32:58.030
And he takes his knife.
于是他拿出了刀。

728
00:32:58.210 --> 00:33:03.410
I was so worried about his leg the whole time, by the way, that he was going to, like, sever his leg.
顺便说一下，我全程都在担心他的腿，怕他会把自己的腿给割伤。

729
00:33:03.590 --> 00:33:04.090
Me too.
我也是。

730
00:33:04.210 --> 00:33:06.690
He cuts his pants into shorts.
他把裤子剪成了短裤。

731
00:33:07.070 --> 00:33:10.130
He then decides to make a hat out of the extra material.
然后他又决定用多余的布料做顶帽子。

732
00:33:10.450 --> 00:33:12.210
His jacket can be a backpack.
他的夹克还能当背包用。

733
00:33:12.690 --> 00:33:15.090
He's just saying the craziest things.
他嘴里一直在说些疯话。

734
00:33:15.450 --> 00:33:17.930
And he has destroyed his pants.
而且他把裤子给毁了。

735
00:33:17.930 --> 00:33:23.710
We got a lot of mail about that scene from Jordan Y., Mary Triggs, and Colby Shannon.
我们收到了很多关于那一幕的来信，来自乔丹·Y、玛丽·特里格斯和科尔比·香农。

736
00:33:23.970 --> 00:33:27.270
They wanted to know, was Steve really cutting his pants?
他们想知道，史蒂夫是真的在剪裤子吗？

737
00:33:27.270 --> 00:33:29.950
Was the costume rigged in some way?
服装是不是做了什么特殊处理？

738
00:33:30.430 --> 00:33:34.570
I reached out to Steve because, like you, Angela, I was very nervous.
我联系了史蒂夫，因为安吉拉，和你一样，我也非常紧张。

739
00:33:34.630 --> 00:33:36.370
It looked very real.
看起来太真实了。

740
00:33:36.870 --> 00:33:40.850
And Steve said the costume was not rigged.
史蒂夫说服装并没有做任何特殊处理。

741
00:33:40.990 --> 00:33:43.510
He cut his pants with a real knife.
他是用真刀剪的裤子。

742
00:33:43.690 --> 00:33:44.670
Shut up!
别开玩笑了！

743
00:33:44.670 --> 00:33:49.650
He said it was, in hindsight, it was a truly stupid thing to do.
他说事后回想起来，那真是个极其愚蠢的举动。

744
00:33:50.190 --> 00:33:53.030
He kind of can't believe that he did it.
他自己都有点不敢相信他当时竟然那么做了。

745
00:33:53.250 --> 00:33:54.630
I cannot believe this.
我简直不敢相信。

746
00:33:54.790 --> 00:33:58.690
We would have a freaking safety meeting for a lit candle.
我们平时点根蜡烛都要开个该死的安全会议。

747
00:33:58.910 --> 00:34:03.730
And now Steve is cutting his pants open in the middle of nowhere, by the way.
结果史蒂夫倒好，在荒郊野外直接拿刀割裤子。

748
00:34:03.910 --> 00:34:06.270
If he did cut his leg, they were far from anything.
如果他真割伤了腿，那地方离哪儿都远。

749
00:34:06.950 --> 00:34:07.190
Yeah.
确实。

750
00:34:07.730 --> 00:34:09.710
Steve really likes this moment, though.
不过史蒂夫本人真的很喜欢这个瞬间。

751
00:34:09.710 --> 00:34:16.470
He said it makes him laugh because in the movie Cast Away, Tom Hanks does this.
他说这让他发笑，因为在电影《荒岛余生》里，汤姆·汉克斯就是这么做的。

752
00:34:16.610 --> 00:34:18.150
And that's kind of where he got the idea.
他的灵感大概就是这么来的。

753
00:34:18.370 --> 00:34:23.210
But Tom Hanks does it after he's been on the deserted island for like two years.
但汤姆·汉克斯是在荒岛上待了大约两年之后才这么做的。

754
00:34:23.410 --> 00:34:23.770
Yeah.
没错。

755
00:34:23.970 --> 00:34:26.070
And Michael does it after 35 minutes.
而迈克尔只用了35分钟就这么做了。

756
00:34:29.390 --> 00:34:31.830
Listen, lady, I think we should take a break.
听着，女士，我觉得我们该休息一下了。

757
00:34:31.830 --> 00:34:35.490
And when we come back, we're going to discuss some cake drama.
等我们回来，我们要讨论一些关于蛋糕的闹剧。

758
00:34:35.810 --> 00:34:36.910
Oh, I can't wait.
哦，我等不及了。

759
00:34:37.170 --> 00:34:40.630
I still can't believe he cut his own pants with that knife.
我还是不敢相信他用那把刀割了自己的裤子。

760
00:34:41.110 --> 00:34:41.730
I know.
我知道。

761
00:34:41.870 --> 00:34:44.290
He specifically told me he did not use stunt legs.
他特意告诉我，他没用替身腿。

762
00:34:44.490 --> 00:34:45.050
Oh, my God.
天哪。

763
00:34:45.530 --> 00:34:47.490
Stunt legs or a stunt knife.
没有替身腿，也没有替身刀。

764
00:34:47.910 --> 00:34:49.830
No stunt legs, no stunt knife.
没有替身腿，没有替身刀。

765
00:34:50.110 --> 00:34:51.790
And no tearaway clothes.
也没有易撕的衣服。

766
00:34:52.050 --> 00:34:53.050
That was all real.
那全都是真的。

767
00:34:53.050 --> 00:35:06.300
We are back and we have cake wars.
我们回来了，现在是蛋糕大战时间。

768
00:35:06.540 --> 00:35:08.300
Cake wars at Dunder Mifflin.
邓德·米夫林的蛋糕大战。

769
00:35:08.720 --> 00:35:11.880
And not the fun kind where they decorate a great cake.
而且不是那种大家一起装饰精美蛋糕的有趣活动。

770
00:35:12.180 --> 00:35:12.700
Exactly.
没错。

771
00:35:13.700 --> 00:35:16.020
No, everyone wants their own cake.
不，每个人都想要自己的蛋糕。

772
00:35:16.260 --> 00:35:18.680
Meredith is like, listen, I want devil's food cake.
梅雷迪思说，听着，我想要恶魔蛋糕。

773
00:35:19.020 --> 00:35:20.060
Jim's like, no problem.
吉姆说，没问题。

774
00:35:20.360 --> 00:35:22.100
And then this ticks off Creed.
然后这就惹恼了克里德。

775
00:35:22.580 --> 00:35:24.840
Creed is like, it is my actual birthday.
克里德说，今天真的是我的生日。

776
00:35:25.180 --> 00:35:26.940
Like, Meredith doesn't get to pick the cake.
梅雷迪思凭什么能选蛋糕？

777
00:35:27.060 --> 00:35:28.340
I don't like devil's food cake.
我不喜欢恶魔蛋糕。

778
00:35:28.480 --> 00:35:29.680
I want peach pie.
我想要桃子派。

779
00:35:29.680 --> 00:35:32.740
I absolutely love Jim and Creed's scene together.
我绝对喜欢吉姆和克里德的那场对手戏。

780
00:35:33.160 --> 00:35:35.220
It's done in this very different style.
它的拍摄风格非常独特。

781
00:35:35.460 --> 00:35:37.500
It looks totally different from any other scene.
看起来和任何其他场景都完全不同。

782
00:35:37.700 --> 00:35:39.340
It's uptight and close.
节奏紧凑，镜头很近。

783
00:35:39.480 --> 00:35:40.280
Creed's super intense.
克里德超级投入。

784
00:35:40.580 --> 00:35:43.580
It reminds me of like an Aaron Sorkin kind of moment where it's like,
这让我想起了艾伦·索金风格的时刻，就像是那种，

785
00:35:43.700 --> 00:35:45.640
rat-tat-tat-tat-tat dialogue back and forth.
机关枪一样快速的对话往来。

786
00:35:45.820 --> 00:35:47.880
And he's like, listen, tell Angela it's for Creed.
他说，听着，告诉安吉拉这是给克里德的。

787
00:35:48.020 --> 00:35:48.780
She'll know what it means.
她会明白是什么意思的。

788
00:35:49.280 --> 00:35:50.860
Can I say something controversial?
我能说点有争议的话吗？

789
00:35:51.560 --> 00:35:52.040
What?
什么？

790
00:35:52.440 --> 00:35:54.100
You don't like Aaron Sorkin?
你不喜欢艾伦·索金？

791
00:35:54.440 --> 00:35:56.000
I love Aaron Sorkin.
我喜欢艾伦·索金。

792
00:35:56.160 --> 00:35:57.900
I don't like peach pie.
我不喜欢桃子派。

793
00:35:58.140 --> 00:35:58.440
Oh!
哦！

794
00:35:58.440 --> 00:36:02.260
I don't like any kind of peach in a dessert.
我不喜欢任何做成甜点的桃子。

795
00:36:02.680 --> 00:36:03.060
Wow.
哇。

796
00:36:03.400 --> 00:36:05.820
I love every other cobbler.
我喜欢其他所有的水果派。

797
00:36:06.000 --> 00:36:09.920
I love berry cobbler, apples, whatever you want to throw in there.
我喜欢浆果派、苹果派，随便你放什么进去都行。

798
00:36:10.100 --> 00:36:11.160
No peaches for me.
但我不要桃子。

799
00:36:11.320 --> 00:36:12.340
I don't know what it is.
我也不知道为什么。

800
00:36:12.400 --> 00:36:16.040
If it's a peach, I want it to stay a peach and I want to eat it as a peach.
如果是桃子，我希望它保持桃子的原样，我想直接吃桃子。

801
00:36:16.180 --> 00:36:18.860
I'm not interested in it being desertified.
我对它变成沙漠化没兴趣。

802
00:36:19.340 --> 00:36:20.160
What is that?
那是什么？

803
00:36:20.160 --> 00:36:20.780
I don't know.
我不知道。

804
00:36:21.060 --> 00:36:22.000
I don't know.
我不知道。

805
00:36:22.240 --> 00:36:23.320
I don't know what that is.
我不知道那是什么。

806
00:36:23.460 --> 00:36:26.060
I mean, do you like, like, do they do peach jam?
我是说，你喜欢，就是，他们会做桃子果酱吗？

807
00:36:26.060 --> 00:36:27.880
I don't want peach as a jam.
我不想要桃子做成的果酱。

808
00:36:28.520 --> 00:36:28.780
Okay.
好吧。

809
00:36:30.180 --> 00:36:32.500
I love how strongly you feel about it.
我很喜欢你对这件事如此强烈的态度。

810
00:36:32.680 --> 00:36:38.640
I have very Angela Martin-esque feelings about how peaches are to be prepared.
我对桃子该怎么处理有着非常安吉拉·马丁式的执念。

811
00:36:38.940 --> 00:36:40.640
Can I share something with you?
我能跟你分享一件事吗？

812
00:36:40.980 --> 00:36:41.420
What?
什么？

813
00:36:41.780 --> 00:36:42.480
Okay, Jenna.
好吧，珍娜。

814
00:36:42.720 --> 00:36:44.840
This is a snarky moment for me.
现在我要开启吐槽模式了。

815
00:36:45.000 --> 00:36:47.440
I'm going to share it with you and everyone listening.
我要把它分享给你和所有听众。

816
00:36:47.940 --> 00:36:48.340
Okay.
好的。

817
00:36:48.580 --> 00:36:51.620
My whole entire life, I'm a summer birthday.
我这辈子，生日都在夏天。

818
00:36:52.220 --> 00:36:56.580
So when I was growing up, they would like have the birthday celebration of whoever at school.
所以我小时候，学校会给过生日的人庆祝。

819
00:36:56.580 --> 00:36:57.780
It was their birthday, right?
轮到谁过生日，对吧？

820
00:36:57.940 --> 00:37:01.840
There'd be like some kind of birthday snack or you'd wear a birthday crown or whatever
会有某种生日零食，或者你会戴上生日皇冠之类的，

821
00:37:01.840 --> 00:37:04.020
it was that your classroom did, right?
你们班级会做的那种，对吧？

822
00:37:04.440 --> 00:37:04.740
Yeah.
是啊。

823
00:37:04.940 --> 00:37:07.340
I never got one because I had a summer birthday.
我从来没得到过，因为我的生日在夏天。

824
00:37:07.480 --> 00:37:08.240
And guess what, guys?
你们猜怎么着，伙计们？

825
00:37:08.400 --> 00:37:13.160
If you grew up in the 70s and 80s, there was no like, this is for all the summer birthday
如果你是在七八十年代长大的，根本没有那种“这是给所有夏天过生日的人”的

826
00:37:13.160 --> 00:37:13.920
celebration.
庆祝活动。

827
00:37:14.200 --> 00:37:15.160
They didn't give a crap.
他们根本不在乎。

828
00:37:15.160 --> 00:37:18.800
You had a summer birthday, you didn't get any kind of celebration at school.
你生日在夏天，你在学校就得不到任何庆祝。

829
00:37:19.160 --> 00:37:22.880
Nowadays, if you have a summer birthday, they do a little thing for the kids with the
现在，如果你的生日在夏天，他们会为夏天过生日的孩子们

830
00:37:22.880 --> 00:37:23.420
summer birthdays.
搞个小仪式。

831
00:37:23.680 --> 00:37:24.660
Not when I was growing up.
但我小时候可没有。

832
00:37:24.920 --> 00:37:27.240
Cut to our time on the office.
转到我们拍《办公室》的时候。

833
00:37:27.540 --> 00:37:28.980
Nine years, Jenna.
九年啊，珍娜。

834
00:37:29.340 --> 00:37:32.960
Nine years, I watched all of you guys get a birthday cake.
九年里，我看着你们所有人都有生日蛋糕。

835
00:37:32.960 --> 00:37:33.460
Oh, no.
噢，不。

836
00:37:33.480 --> 00:37:39.720
I watched the whole entire cast and crew gather around and clap and sing happy birthday and
我看着整个剧组和工作人员聚在一起，鼓掌、唱生日歌，

837
00:37:39.720 --> 00:37:40.500
take pictures.
还拍照留念。

838
00:37:40.780 --> 00:37:44.220
And Peter and Vartan would make a special cake for the birthday person.
而且彼得和瓦尔坦会为过生日的人专门做一个蛋糕。

839
00:37:44.220 --> 00:37:45.380
Seven, nine years.
七年，九年。

840
00:37:45.900 --> 00:37:46.140
Yep.
没错。

841
00:37:46.420 --> 00:37:48.740
We never shot The Office in June, did we, Angela?
我们从来没在六月拍过《办公室》，对吧，安吉拉？

842
00:37:48.980 --> 00:37:50.280
Never shot The Office in June.
从来没在六月拍过《办公室》。

843
00:37:50.440 --> 00:37:52.820
Guess who never got the office birthday cake?
猜猜谁从来没拿到过办公室的生日蛋糕？

844
00:37:52.980 --> 00:37:53.520
Oh, no.
噢，不。

845
00:37:53.780 --> 00:37:54.060
Me.
我。

846
00:37:54.260 --> 00:37:54.700
Oh, God.
天哪。

847
00:37:54.800 --> 00:37:55.680
I never got it.
我从来没得到过。

848
00:37:55.800 --> 00:37:56.200
Oh, no.
噢，不。

849
00:37:56.300 --> 00:37:57.100
I never got it.
我从来没得到过。

850
00:37:57.360 --> 00:38:01.860
I remember like around season eight, they rolled out a cake for someone.
我记得大概在第八季的时候，他们给某个人推出来一个蛋糕。

851
00:38:02.040 --> 00:38:03.100
Everyone's clapping and singing.
大家都在鼓掌唱歌。

852
00:38:03.620 --> 00:38:06.980
And I literally said out loud, no one ever did this for me.
我当时真的大声说出来，从来没人为我做过这种事。

853
00:38:11.770 --> 00:38:14.590
And someone else was like, yeah, I have a summer birthday.
然后另一个人就说，是啊，我的生日也在夏天。

854
00:38:14.950 --> 00:38:16.650
Where's our summer birthday cake?
那我们的夏日生日蛋糕呢？

855
00:38:17.010 --> 00:38:18.630
Did they ever do it?
他们有做过吗？

856
00:38:18.890 --> 00:38:19.170
No.
没有。

857
00:38:19.390 --> 00:38:22.250
I have never gotten a birthday cake at school or work.
我从来没在学校或公司收到过生日蛋糕。

858
00:38:22.450 --> 00:38:23.890
This is my Crimea River.
这就是我的“克里米亚河”（意指：这就是我的伤心事）。

859
00:38:24.110 --> 00:38:29.630
But when I see these scenes, I just remember like being like, yeah, well, where's my f***ing
但每当我看到这些场景，我就想起当时心想，是啊，那我的那个该死的

860
00:38:29.630 --> 00:38:29.910
cake?
蛋糕呢？

861
00:38:30.290 --> 00:38:31.170
Oh, my God.
天哪。

862
00:38:31.690 --> 00:38:33.010
Lady, I'm so sorry.
这位女士，我太抱歉了。

863
00:38:33.010 --> 00:38:34.030
You're right.
你说得对。

864
00:38:34.270 --> 00:38:39.930
I enjoyed many a March birthday cake by Peter and Vartan with the candles.
我享受过很多次彼得和瓦尔坦为我准备的三月生日蛋糕，还有蜡烛。

865
00:38:40.150 --> 00:38:44.150
Sometimes they would do a photo cake and put some sweet personal photo on it.
有时他们会做照片蛋糕，把一些温馨的个人照片印在上面。

866
00:38:44.470 --> 00:38:49.290
Jenna, I have multiple photos I took of other people in their cakes.
珍娜，我拍过很多别人吃蛋糕的照片。

867
00:38:49.990 --> 00:38:50.630
Oh, no.
噢，不。

868
00:38:51.230 --> 00:38:53.470
We also did it for the crew members.
我们也会为剧组成员这样做。

869
00:38:53.750 --> 00:38:54.290
I know.
我知道。

870
00:38:54.670 --> 00:38:55.050
Yeah.
是啊。

871
00:38:55.510 --> 00:38:56.230
Summer birthdays.
夏日生日的人。

872
00:38:56.610 --> 00:38:57.170
S-O-L.
只能自求多福了。

873
00:38:57.770 --> 00:39:00.370
So, listen, I turned 50 in June.
听着，我六月份就满五十岁了。

874
00:39:00.370 --> 00:39:05.510
I expect an office lady's birthday cake and a song and applause.
我期待能有一个办公室女职员的生日蛋糕，还有歌声和掌声。

875
00:39:06.750 --> 00:39:07.010
Okay.
好的。

876
00:39:07.490 --> 00:39:07.870
Done.
没问题。

877
00:39:08.090 --> 00:39:10.250
Did you get that, Sam, Cassie, Cody?
山姆、凯西、科迪，你们听到了吗？

878
00:39:10.770 --> 00:39:13.550
For once in my life, I want a work birthday.
我这辈子头一次，想要一个在工作中度过的生日。

879
00:39:14.090 --> 00:39:15.110
You know what, Angela?
你知道吗，安吉拉？

880
00:39:15.290 --> 00:39:21.150
I promise we will not take a vacation the week of your birthday just so that we are forced
我保证我们不会在你生日那周去度假，这样我们就不得不

881
00:39:21.150 --> 00:39:22.050
to celebrate it.
为你庆祝了。

882
00:39:22.210 --> 00:39:23.830
I want to work on my birthday.
我想在生日那天工作。

883
00:39:23.890 --> 00:39:24.850
Yeah, that's the other thing.
是啊，还有一点。

884
00:39:25.170 --> 00:39:28.430
Everyone else is like, dude, at least you were like on vacation for your birthday.
其他人总说，老兄，至少你生日那天在度假啊。

885
00:39:28.430 --> 00:39:29.410
I was stuck at work.
我却被困在工作中。

886
00:39:29.410 --> 00:39:30.350
At least I got a cake.
至少我得到了一个蛋糕。

887
00:39:31.750 --> 00:39:33.970
I want to work on my birthday and I want a cake.
我想在生日那天工作，而且我想要一个蛋糕。

888
00:39:34.270 --> 00:39:36.430
We'll make that happen for you this year, Angela.
安吉拉，今年我们会为你实现的。

889
00:39:36.570 --> 00:39:36.970
I promise.
我保证。

890
00:39:37.330 --> 00:39:37.790
Thank you.
谢谢。

891
00:39:37.970 --> 00:39:39.190
I really appreciate it.
我真的很感激。

892
00:39:39.530 --> 00:39:42.530
Should we talk about Andy's cake demand?
我们要聊聊安迪对蛋糕的要求吗？

893
00:39:43.190 --> 00:39:43.670
Yes.
好的。

894
00:39:44.070 --> 00:39:49.590
He wants a Fudgy the Whale ice cream cake and pizza rolls and mushroom caps.
他想要一个“Fudgy the Whale”冰淇淋蛋糕，还要披萨卷和蘑菇盖。

895
00:39:50.010 --> 00:39:50.910
Oh, lady.
噢，天哪。

896
00:39:51.170 --> 00:39:53.310
Do you remember the Fudgy the Whale?
你还记得“Fudgy the Whale”吗？

897
00:39:53.470 --> 00:39:54.870
Do you remember this on set?
你记得片场有这个吗？

898
00:39:55.110 --> 00:39:56.030
It was a big deal.
那可是件大事。

899
00:39:56.030 --> 00:39:56.970
I do.
我记得。

900
00:39:57.250 --> 00:39:59.670
Because it's a special cake brand.
因为那是一个特别的蛋糕品牌。

901
00:40:00.010 --> 00:40:00.490
Yes.
是的。

902
00:40:00.650 --> 00:40:01.750
It's Carvel, right?
是卡维尔（Carvel）对吧？

903
00:40:01.890 --> 00:40:07.470
And I had never heard of Fudgy the Whale, which I remember a few of the crew and cast were
我以前从没听说过“鲸鱼法吉”（Fudgy the Whale），我记得当时剧组里的一些人

904
00:40:07.470 --> 00:40:08.510
like, are you kidding me?
就像是说，你在开玩笑吗？

905
00:40:08.510 --> 00:40:10.050
You've never heard of Fudgy the Whale?
你居然没听说过鲸鱼法吉？

906
00:40:10.190 --> 00:40:11.690
But it was an East Coast thing.
但这其实是东海岸那边的东西。

907
00:40:11.990 --> 00:40:13.050
I'd never heard of it.
我确实没听说过。

908
00:40:13.170 --> 00:40:14.570
It's totally an East Coast thing.
这绝对是东海岸的特色。

909
00:40:14.790 --> 00:40:19.290
Well, last night, somebody might have done what she likes to call a mini dive.
嗯，昨晚，有人可能做了一次她所谓的“迷你潜水”。

910
00:40:19.830 --> 00:40:21.830
Oh, you mini dived Fudgy the Whale.
噢，你对鲸鱼法吉做了“迷你潜水”。

911
00:40:21.830 --> 00:40:24.870
I mean, that does sound inappropriate, but I like it.
我是说，这听起来确实不太合适，但我喜欢。

912
00:40:25.890 --> 00:40:26.710
There you go.
这就对了。

913
00:40:27.150 --> 00:40:27.450
All right.
好吧。

914
00:40:27.570 --> 00:40:30.570
Here's everything you need to know about Fudgy the Whale.
关于鲸鱼法吉，你需要知道的一切都在这儿了。

915
00:40:31.070 --> 00:40:34.810
Carvel was founded by Tom Carvel, who, by the way, is fascinating.
卡维尔是由汤姆·卡维尔创立的，顺便说一句，他这个人非常迷人。

916
00:40:35.070 --> 00:40:39.450
That would be a whole other deep dive about his life and how he really gave birth to like
那得是关于他生平的另一场深度挖掘了，讲讲他是如何真正催生了

917
00:40:39.450 --> 00:40:41.690
this whole franchise ice cream phenomenon.
整个连锁冰淇淋现象的。

918
00:40:41.970 --> 00:40:43.770
But here's the famous story.
但这里有个著名的故事。

919
00:40:43.970 --> 00:40:44.670
It's on their website.
在他们的官网上有写。

920
00:40:44.830 --> 00:40:46.230
It's in multiple places online.
网上很多地方都能找到。

921
00:40:46.910 --> 00:40:51.950
Legend has it, Tom Carvel had an ice cream truck that broke down and his ice cream started
传说汤姆·卡维尔有一辆冰淇淋车坏了，他的冰淇淋开始

922
00:40:51.950 --> 00:40:52.450
to melt.
融化了。

923
00:40:52.630 --> 00:40:56.030
So he was really trying quickly to sell off all this ice cream before it melted.
所以他当时真的很着急，想在冰淇淋融化前赶紧卖掉。

924
00:40:56.030 --> 00:40:59.850
And he found that the customers actually liked it soft.
结果他发现顾客其实很喜欢软冰淇淋。

925
00:41:00.170 --> 00:41:02.450
So he was like, wait a second.
于是他心想，等等。

926
00:41:02.530 --> 00:41:07.190
And he started serving soft serve ice cream and no one else was doing that.
他开始供应软冰淇淋，当时还没人这么做过。

927
00:41:07.390 --> 00:41:07.670
Oh.
噢。

928
00:41:07.870 --> 00:41:10.330
And so it became a whole thing, right?
然后这事儿就火了，对吧？

929
00:41:10.490 --> 00:41:12.470
He developed a soft serve ice cream machine.
他研发了一台软冰淇淋机。

930
00:41:12.630 --> 00:41:13.710
He even patented it.
甚至还申请了专利。

931
00:41:13.830 --> 00:41:15.150
He sold it to other franchises.
他把它卖给了其他加盟商。

932
00:41:15.150 --> 00:41:17.730
Because this man, Jenna, he was a boss lady.
因为这个男人，珍娜，他真是个霸道总裁。

933
00:41:17.870 --> 00:41:18.730
He was a boss dude.
他是个霸道大叔。

934
00:41:18.890 --> 00:41:19.710
He was a boss daddy.
他是个霸道老爹。

935
00:41:19.970 --> 00:41:20.510
There we go.
这就对了。

936
00:41:20.570 --> 00:41:21.430
He was a boss daddy.
他是个霸道老爹。

937
00:41:22.010 --> 00:41:27.970
And he started the very first Carvel ice cream shop on the exact spot where his truck
他在他那辆车坏掉的那个地方，

938
00:41:27.970 --> 00:41:28.590
broke down.
开了第一家卡维尔冰淇淋店。

939
00:41:29.150 --> 00:41:30.570
That is boss daddy.
那真是太霸道老爹了。

940
00:41:31.270 --> 00:41:33.150
So there are Carvel stores.
所以现在有卡维尔门店了。

941
00:41:33.270 --> 00:41:33.890
They're franchised.
它们是加盟店。

942
00:41:33.990 --> 00:41:35.930
There is one now in Los Angeles, Jenna.
洛杉矶现在就有一家，珍娜。

943
00:41:36.410 --> 00:41:36.730
Really?
真的吗？

944
00:41:37.070 --> 00:41:39.670
There used to not be, but there is one now in Los Angeles.
以前没有，但现在洛杉矶有一家了。

945
00:41:39.670 --> 00:41:43.530
And they became famous for a few cakes.
他们因为几款蛋糕而出名。

946
00:41:43.850 --> 00:41:48.150
In the 70s, they created this cake called the cookie puss.
在70年代，他们创造了一款叫“曲奇脸”（Cookie Puss）的蛋糕。

947
00:41:48.430 --> 00:41:49.090
Oh, boy.
天哪。

948
00:41:49.430 --> 00:41:49.850
I know.
我知道。

949
00:41:50.170 --> 00:41:51.230
The hug me bear.
还有“拥抱熊”（Hug Me Bear）。

950
00:41:51.490 --> 00:41:55.810
And then Fudgy the Whale followed in June of 1977.
然后鲸鱼法吉是在1977年6月推出的。

951
00:41:55.970 --> 00:41:58.130
He was all Tom Carvel's idea.
这全都是汤姆·卡维尔的主意。

952
00:41:58.430 --> 00:42:00.610
He was like, we need a cake for Father's Day.
他说，我们需要一个父亲节蛋糕。

953
00:42:00.610 --> 00:42:02.210
I want it to be a whale.
我想要一个鲸鱼形状的。

954
00:42:02.210 --> 00:42:05.590
And I want the slogan to say, for a whale of a dad.
而且我希望标语写着：送给超棒的爸爸。

955
00:42:06.110 --> 00:42:07.050
Oh, my God.
天哪。

956
00:42:07.050 --> 00:42:09.190
I am loving so much about this.
我太喜欢这个点子了。

957
00:42:09.750 --> 00:42:11.290
I looked up the expression.
我查了一下这个表达。

958
00:42:11.290 --> 00:42:13.590
I'd never heard of this, a whale of a something.
我以前从没听过“a whale of a something”这种说法。

959
00:42:13.810 --> 00:42:15.270
I don't know if you've heard of that expression.
不知道你有没有听过这个表达。

960
00:42:15.410 --> 00:42:15.790
I hadn't.
我没听过。

961
00:42:15.890 --> 00:42:17.230
But that was an expression.
但确实有这种说法。

962
00:42:17.490 --> 00:42:21.450
And it referred to a very great amount of something or a very good thing.
它指的是非常多或者非常好的东西。

963
00:42:21.690 --> 00:42:25.450
So to be a whale of a dad was, you were a great dad, right?
所以“a whale of a dad”就是指你是个很棒的爸爸，对吧？

964
00:42:25.890 --> 00:42:27.510
Fudgy the Whale was so successful.
“鲸鱼法吉”大获成功。

965
00:42:27.510 --> 00:42:28.770
They kept the mold.
他们保留了模具。

966
00:42:28.970 --> 00:42:31.030
And talk about reuse, repurpose.
说到重复利用和再利用。

967
00:42:31.030 --> 00:42:35.650
At Christmastime, they flipped Fudgy the Whale on its head and made his tail like the
到了圣诞节，他们把“鲸鱼法吉”倒过来，把它的尾巴做成

968
00:42:35.650 --> 00:42:39.270
Santa hat and made him into a Santa.
圣诞帽，把它变成了圣诞老人。

969
00:42:39.530 --> 00:42:41.970
And to this day, you can still get Fudgy the Whale.
直到今天，你依然可以买到“鲸鱼法吉”。

970
00:42:42.010 --> 00:42:44.370
And you can also get a female Fudgy the Whale.
而且你还可以买到雌性的“鲸鱼法吉”。

971
00:42:44.510 --> 00:42:48.230
They'll give her pink piping and like eyelashes and a little bow.
他们会给它加上粉色的装饰边，还有睫毛和一个小蝴蝶结。

972
00:42:48.570 --> 00:42:52.810
And more than 50,000 Fudgy the Whale ice cream cakes are sold every year.
每年有超过五万个“鲸鱼法吉”冰淇淋蛋糕被售出。

973
00:42:53.170 --> 00:42:57.970
All the cakes come with two layers of chocolate and vanilla separated by a layer of what they
所有的蛋糕都有两层巧克力和香草，中间隔着一层他们称之为

974
00:42:57.970 --> 00:42:58.850
call crunchies.
“脆脆”的东西。

975
00:42:58.990 --> 00:43:00.850
They don't tell you what's in their crunchy recipe.
他们不会告诉你“脆脆”配方里有什么。

976
00:43:01.030 --> 00:43:05.450
And you can customize it with favorite flavors and a different type of center.
而且你可以用喜欢的口味和不同类型的夹心来定制它。

977
00:43:05.690 --> 00:43:07.010
And there you have it.
事情就是这样。

978
00:43:07.110 --> 00:43:07.990
That's Fudgy the Whale.
这就是“鲸鱼法吉”。

979
00:43:08.170 --> 00:43:10.350
But I have one other thing I want to play you.
但我还有另一件事想放给你听。

980
00:43:10.710 --> 00:43:14.810
Tom Carvel himself would do all the jingles and commercials for Fudgy the Whale.
汤姆·卡维尔本人会为“鲸鱼法吉”录制所有的广告歌和广告词。

981
00:43:15.010 --> 00:43:15.890
No way!
不会吧！

982
00:43:16.070 --> 00:43:16.270
Yeah.
是真的。

983
00:43:16.590 --> 00:43:17.070
All right, Jenna.
好的，珍娜。

984
00:43:17.210 --> 00:43:20.350
Here's Tom Carvel talking about Fudgy the Whale for their ad.
这是汤姆·卡维尔为“鲸鱼法吉”录制的广告。

985
00:43:22.290 --> 00:43:24.030
Fudgy the Whale is back.
“鲸鱼法吉”回归了。

986
00:43:24.230 --> 00:43:26.610
That's a whale of a cake for a whale of a dad.
这是送给超棒爸爸的超棒蛋糕。

987
00:43:26.790 --> 00:43:29.250
But you participate in Carvel Ice Cream Store.
但你得去卡维尔冰淇淋店参与活动。

988
00:43:29.390 --> 00:43:29.490
Yup.
没错。

989
00:43:29.750 --> 00:43:33.250
And this year, your Carvel dealer makes you loaded with fudge and nuts.
今年，你的卡维尔经销商会为你准备满满的软糖和坚果。

990
00:43:33.690 --> 00:43:37.430
And you can get Fudgy with an ocean to serve 20 people.
你还可以买到能供20人享用的“鲸鱼法吉”。

991
00:43:37.690 --> 00:43:42.910
But if you want to send Fudgy the Whale to a whale of a dad, anywhere in the Carvel territory,
但如果你想在卡维尔的任何服务区域，给超棒的爸爸送去“鲸鱼法吉”，

992
00:43:42.910 --> 00:43:45.390
you call the phone number that you see here.
请拨打屏幕上的电话号码。

993
00:43:45.570 --> 00:43:46.230
Thank you.
谢谢。

994
00:43:46.650 --> 00:43:48.050
And have a happy day, Dad.
祝爸爸们节日快乐。

995
00:43:50.150 --> 00:43:53.990
I don't want to tip my hand too much.
我不想过早透露我的意图。

996
00:43:54.170 --> 00:43:56.650
Am I going to get a Fudgy the Whale for my 50th birthday?
我50岁生日的时候能收到一个“鲸鱼法吉”吗？

997
00:43:57.090 --> 00:43:59.890
How could we not get you a Fudgy the Whale now?
现在我们怎么可能不给你买一个“鲸鱼法吉”呢？

998
00:44:00.190 --> 00:44:01.090
Oh my God.
天哪。

999
00:44:01.090 --> 00:44:03.130
I am so excited already.
我已经兴奋得不行了。

1000
00:44:04.150 --> 00:44:07.310
I want to eat one of those so bad now that you've described it.
听你描述完，我现在特别想吃一个。

1001
00:44:07.630 --> 00:44:08.290
I know.
我知道。

1002
00:44:08.430 --> 00:44:09.630
I went on Carvel's website.
我上了Carvel的网站。

1003
00:44:09.770 --> 00:44:11.130
There's so many cool looking cakes.
上面有很多看起来很酷的蛋糕。

1004
00:44:11.290 --> 00:44:12.590
They do a lot more now.
他们现在做的种类多多了。

1005
00:44:12.810 --> 00:44:13.670
I'm not going to lie.
说实话。

1006
00:44:13.770 --> 00:44:15.250
The cookie puss is kind of odd looking.
那个“饼干猫脸”（Cookie Puss）看起来有点怪。

1007
00:44:17.110 --> 00:44:17.550
What?
什么？

1008
00:44:17.710 --> 00:44:18.370
Is it a cat?
那是只猫吗？

1009
00:44:18.710 --> 00:44:20.050
I took a picture of it.
我拍了张照片。

1010
00:44:20.170 --> 00:44:23.710
Here were their first three cakes that were like their famous cakes.
这是他们最初的三款招牌蛋糕。

1011
00:44:24.170 --> 00:44:24.610
Okay.
好吧。

1012
00:44:24.750 --> 00:44:26.050
I can't wait for you to see this.
我等不及要让你看看这个了。

1013
00:44:27.710 --> 00:44:29.310
This is the cookie puss.
这就是“饼干猫脸”。

1014
00:44:29.550 --> 00:44:29.990
Oh.
噢。

1015
00:44:29.990 --> 00:44:33.330
Well, it has a full ice cream cone as a nose.
你看，它用一个完整的冰淇淋甜筒当鼻子。

1016
00:44:33.570 --> 00:44:33.790
Yeah.
是啊。

1017
00:44:34.330 --> 00:44:37.850
And then on its cheeks, it has little arms drawn on.
然后它的脸颊上还画着小胳膊。

1018
00:44:37.970 --> 00:44:39.270
It has cookies for eyes.
它的眼睛是饼干做的。

1019
00:44:39.530 --> 00:44:40.550
Are they arms?
那是胳膊吗？

1020
00:44:41.210 --> 00:44:42.510
What's the puss part?
“Puss”那部分是什么意思？

1021
00:44:42.970 --> 00:44:45.190
Is it meant to be a cat?
它是想做成猫的样子吗？

1022
00:44:45.370 --> 00:44:46.130
I don't know.
我不知道。

1023
00:44:46.250 --> 00:44:47.490
I don't understand what it is.
我搞不懂那到底是什么。

1024
00:44:47.650 --> 00:44:48.550
Here's the best part.
最精彩的部分来了。

1025
00:44:48.870 --> 00:44:53.430
For St. Patrick's Day, you can get a cookie opuss, the Irish version.
圣帕特里克节的时候，你可以买到“饼干爱尔兰猫脸”（Cookie O'Puss），就是爱尔兰版本。

1026
00:44:55.370 --> 00:44:56.830
I don't understand it.
我还是搞不懂。

1027
00:44:56.830 --> 00:44:57.990
I want to eat it.
我想吃它。

1028
00:44:58.090 --> 00:44:58.650
I don't know.
我不知道。

1029
00:44:58.650 --> 00:45:01.970
I went real deep onto the Carvel site, but I'm very excited.
我深入研究了Carvel的网站，但我真的很兴奋。

1030
00:45:02.170 --> 00:45:04.330
I want to fudge you the whale for my 50th birthday.
我50岁生日时想吃那个“软糖鲸鱼”蛋糕。

1031
00:45:04.690 --> 00:45:05.110
Done.
成交。

1032
00:45:06.010 --> 00:45:07.030
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

1033
00:45:07.270 --> 00:45:09.550
I don't remember it being on set.
我不记得片场出现过它。

1034
00:45:09.750 --> 00:45:10.390
Isn't that funny?
那难道不好笑吗？

1035
00:45:10.530 --> 00:45:15.150
I remember everyone talking about it, and I remember people saying, what is it?
我记得大家都在讨论它，也记得有人问那是什么。

1036
00:45:15.270 --> 00:45:17.990
But I don't remember ever having one.
但我完全不记得自己吃过。

1037
00:45:18.390 --> 00:45:20.130
I totally remember it.
我完全记得。

1038
00:45:20.270 --> 00:45:24.110
I mean, my character didn't eat it, but I remember Ed eating it in the scene.
我是说，我的角色没吃，但我记得埃德在戏里吃过。

1039
00:45:24.110 --> 00:45:24.950
Wow.
哇。

1040
00:45:25.450 --> 00:45:25.570
Wow.
哇。

1041
00:45:25.570 --> 00:45:28.710
Well, when we eat your cake for your birthday, it's going to be all new to me.
好吧，等你过生日吃蛋糕的时候，对我来说一切都是全新的体验。

1042
00:45:30.390 --> 00:45:33.410
Ladies, should we go back out into the wilderness?
女士们，我们要回到荒野中去了吗？

1043
00:45:34.010 --> 00:45:35.670
Oh, definitely we should.
噢，当然要。

1044
00:45:35.970 --> 00:45:40.050
I have a crew catch at 13 minutes, 15 seconds.
我在13分15秒处发现了一个穿帮镜头。

1045
00:45:40.430 --> 00:45:41.490
Oh, what'd you catch?
噢，你发现了什么？

1046
00:45:41.490 --> 00:45:48.550
You can see our cinematographer Randall Einhorn's hand come into frame and brush some tree branches
你可以看到我们的摄影师兰德尔·艾因霍恩的手伸进画面，拨开了几根树枝，

1047
00:45:48.550 --> 00:45:51.510
away that were probably going to hit his camera.
那些树枝可能要碰到他的摄像机了。

1048
00:45:51.730 --> 00:45:53.450
He's walking behind Dwight.
他当时正跟在德怀特身后走。

1049
00:45:54.070 --> 00:45:55.910
Oh, Jenna, that's a great catch.
噢，珍娜，你观察得真仔细。

1050
00:45:55.910 --> 00:45:56.930
I didn't see that.
我没注意到。

1051
00:45:57.070 --> 00:45:57.890
What's the time code?
时间码是多少？

1052
00:45:57.890 --> 00:46:00.370
13 minutes, 15 seconds.
13分15秒。

1053
00:46:00.710 --> 00:46:05.650
I was not the only person to catch it, but I want to say that I saw it before I saw our
并不是只有我一个人发现了，但我得说，我在看到我们的

1054
00:46:05.650 --> 00:46:06.050
mail.
邮件之前就注意到了。

1055
00:46:06.490 --> 00:46:13.570
But Tim Wong, Jonah T, Addie H, and Kiana Raber also wrote in about Randall's hand.
不过Tim Wong、Jonah T、Addie H和Kiana Raber也写信提到了Randall的手。

1056
00:46:13.870 --> 00:46:15.250
Well, great job, guys.
好吧，干得好，各位。

1057
00:46:15.390 --> 00:46:15.890
Great job.
干得漂亮。

1058
00:46:16.270 --> 00:46:23.410
We also had Jasper Anders and Morgan Elridge write in to ask, what did Phil Shea use for
Jasper Anders和Morgan Elridge也写信问，Phil Shea用什么做的

1059
00:46:23.410 --> 00:46:26.950
the bird eggs that Dwight finds and cooks?
Dwight找到并煮熟的鸟蛋？

1060
00:46:26.950 --> 00:46:30.130
They kind of look like they might be small potatoes.
它们看起来有点像小土豆。

1061
00:46:30.570 --> 00:46:31.330
Guess what?
你猜怎么着？

1062
00:46:32.030 --> 00:46:32.370
What?
什么？

1063
00:46:33.010 --> 00:46:34.450
They were small potatoes.
它们就是小土豆。

1064
00:46:35.110 --> 00:46:35.630
Really?
真的吗？

1065
00:46:36.090 --> 00:46:38.950
Teeny tiny potatoes meant to look like eggs.
用来冒充鸟蛋的迷你小土豆。

1066
00:46:39.310 --> 00:46:43.750
I totally thought they were eggs, but I was trying to think what kind of bird makes a
我完全以为那是鸟蛋，但我一直在想，什么样的鸟会

1067
00:46:43.750 --> 00:46:45.030
nest like that up in a tree.
在树上筑那样的巢。

1068
00:46:47.360 --> 00:46:47.580
What?
什么？

1069
00:46:50.240 --> 00:46:51.180
Many birds?
很多鸟？

1070
00:46:51.840 --> 00:46:52.760
So many birds?
很多很多的鸟？

1071
00:46:52.980 --> 00:46:54.860
That was such a big nest, though.
不过那巢确实很大。

1072
00:46:54.860 --> 00:46:58.360
So, like, those eggs look like a bird that would, like, lay them on the ground to me.
所以，我觉得那些蛋看起来像是那种会把蛋下在地上的鸟下的。

1073
00:47:00.120 --> 00:47:03.940
Or, I mean, I guess, what?
或者，我是说，我想，什么？

1074
00:47:06.780 --> 00:47:11.560
Or maybe they're the eggs of a bird that would nest really up high.
或者它们可能是那种在高处筑巢的鸟下的蛋。

1075
00:47:12.020 --> 00:47:12.420
Exactly.
没错。

1076
00:47:12.840 --> 00:47:15.840
They didn't look like the type of eggs that you could just reach with your hand.
它们看起来不像是那种你伸手就能拿到的蛋。

1077
00:47:16.020 --> 00:47:19.360
I think you would either find them on the ground or they'd be up on a cliff top.
我觉得你要么会在地上找到它们，要么它们会在悬崖顶上。

1078
00:47:19.620 --> 00:47:22.060
I think that that's a good way to say it.
我觉得这样说很贴切。

1079
00:47:24.260 --> 00:47:31.900
When you said, what kind of bird lays eggs in a tree, I was confused.
当你问什么样的鸟会在树上产卵时，我当时很困惑。

1080
00:47:32.240 --> 00:47:36.440
But I'm hearing your point now, and I hear it, and I think it's a good point.
但我现在听懂你的意思了，我明白了，我觉得你说得很有道理。

1081
00:47:36.440 --> 00:47:37.340
Thank you.
谢谢你。

1082
00:47:37.540 --> 00:47:42.420
I need to talk about this shot of Michael singing happy birthday because it is just
我得谈谈Michael唱生日歌的那个镜头，因为它简直

1083
00:47:42.420 --> 00:47:42.880
wonderful.
太棒了。

1084
00:47:43.360 --> 00:47:43.520
Oh.
哦。

1085
00:47:43.800 --> 00:47:45.580
Michael has just made a spear.
Michael刚做了一把长矛。

1086
00:47:46.020 --> 00:47:50.580
The teeniest, tiniest spear on the end of a very crooked stick.
在一根非常弯曲的棍子末端，绑着一把极小极小的长矛。

1087
00:47:50.860 --> 00:47:55.920
I want to point out that he made a spear when he has an amazing knife, like you would think
我想指出的是，他明明有一把很棒的刀，却做了把长矛，你本来会以为

1088
00:47:55.920 --> 00:47:58.360
he would attach the knife to the end of the stick.
他会把刀绑在棍子末端的。

1089
00:47:58.600 --> 00:47:59.880
With his duct tape.
用他的强力胶带。

1090
00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:00.800
With his duct tape.
用他的强力胶带。

1091
00:48:00.800 --> 00:48:06.440
He might have used all his duct tape to fashion his tent out of his pants.
他可能把所有的强力胶带都用来把裤子改造成帐篷了。

1092
00:48:06.440 --> 00:48:07.880
That's coming up, I guess.
我想那段情节快到了。

1093
00:48:08.180 --> 00:48:12.580
But yeah, there's this shot that pulls so far back.
不过，确实，那个镜头拉得非常远。

1094
00:48:12.800 --> 00:48:19.320
And what's amazing about it to me is, guys, Steve was really in the middle of nowhere.
最让我惊叹的是，伙计们，Steve当时真的是在荒郊野外。

1095
00:48:19.320 --> 00:48:24.080
And our crew was far back as this shot reveals.
而且正如镜头所展示的那样，我们的摄制组离得很远。

1096
00:48:24.840 --> 00:48:25.020
Yeah.
是啊。

1097
00:48:25.020 --> 00:48:27.200
I thought it was a beautiful shot.
我觉得那是一个很美的镜头。

1098
00:48:27.400 --> 00:48:34.260
I also love these moments when Michael remembers things like sprinkles, like Creed's birthday,
我也很喜欢Michael记得像Sprinkles、Creed的生日这些事的时刻，

1099
00:48:34.820 --> 00:48:37.520
you know, when he sings a song and he's like, happy birthday, buddy.
