Anyway, that is the download on the mushrooMs.
总之，关于蘑菇的情况就是这样。

1256
00:56:06.520 --> 00:56:09.200
Well, you know the scene where Dwight tackles Michael to the ground?
对了，你记得德怀特把迈克尔扑倒在地的那一幕吗？

1257
00:56:09.700 --> 00:56:09.840
Yeah.
记得。

1258
00:56:10.080 --> 00:56:12.860
There was much more of this in the deleted scenes.
删减片段里还有很多相关内容。

1259
00:56:12.860 --> 00:56:18.040
There is a great talking head where Michael's like, you know, when Dwight tackled me to
有一个很棒的采访镜头，迈克尔说，你知道吗，当德怀特把我扑倒在

1260
00:56:18.040 --> 00:56:22.440
the ground and was fishing the mushrooms out of my mouth with his finger.
地上，用手指从我嘴里抠蘑菇的时候。

1261
00:56:22.720 --> 00:56:23.820
He says it.
他就是这么说的。

1262
00:56:23.940 --> 00:56:25.740
He's like, when Dwight had his finger in my mouth.
他说，当德怀特把手指伸进我嘴里的时候。

1263
00:56:25.840 --> 00:56:31.580
He said, I laid back and I looked at the sky and the birds were chirping and there were clouds
他说，我躺在那儿看着天空，鸟儿在鸣叫，云朵在飘浮，

1264
00:56:31.580 --> 00:56:33.060
and it was so beautiful.
一切都太美好了。

1265
00:56:33.440 --> 00:56:36.680
And then I vomited because it was really gross.
然后我就吐了，因为那真的很恶心。

1266
00:56:37.020 --> 00:56:41.800
It's really funny that he had this sort of beautiful moment while Dwight was trying to fish
他能在德怀特试图从他嘴里抠出蘑菇时，产生这种美好的瞬间，真是太搞笑了。

1267
00:56:41.800 --> 00:56:43.160
the mushrooms out of his mouth.
（抠蘑菇）

1268
00:56:43.360 --> 00:56:49.120
I have to ask, is that talking head, is he wearing his torn up clothes or is he wearing
我得问问，那个采访镜头里，他穿的是那件破烂的衣服，还是穿的

1269
00:56:49.120 --> 00:56:50.460
Dwight's sweatshirt?
德怀特的运动衫？

1270
00:56:50.460 --> 00:56:54.720
No, it would have been like a wrap up talking head about his day.
不，那应该是他一天结束后的总结采访。

1271
00:56:54.720 --> 00:56:58.500
And he was in his office with the Battlestar Galactica sweatshirt.
当时他在办公室里，穿着那件《太空堡垒卡拉狄加》的运动衫。

1272
00:56:58.680 --> 00:57:02.540
Well, I love this idea that his clothes are tattered.
好吧，我喜欢他衣服破破烂烂的设定。

1273
00:57:02.740 --> 00:57:04.460
He's probably vomited on them.
他可能已经在上面吐过了。

1274
00:57:04.580 --> 00:57:09.100
And Dwight has to give him this rescue sweatshirt that was in his trunk.
所以德怀特不得不把后备箱里的备用运动衫给他穿。

1275
00:57:10.220 --> 00:57:15.720
Well, Jenna, I want you to know at 18 minutes, 31 seconds, when Dwight and Michael come back
珍娜，我想让你知道，在18分31秒时，当德怀特和迈克尔回来

1276
00:57:15.720 --> 00:57:20.040
and they walk in the party and Michael immediately starts hitting those high notes, right?
走进派对现场，迈克尔立刻开始唱起高音，对吧？

1277
00:57:20.040 --> 00:57:21.220
He doesn't miss a beat.
他一点都没跑调。

1278
00:57:21.420 --> 00:57:27.560
The camera pans the conference room and Toby, Pam, Angela, and Oscar are all standing together
镜头扫过会议室，托比、帕姆、安吉拉和奥斯卡都站在一起，

1279
00:57:27.560 --> 00:57:30.220
and they are smiling so big.
他们笑得特别开心。

1280
00:57:30.380 --> 00:57:36.120
And I thought, oh my God, Toby and Angela are happy to see Michael and Oscar.
我当时想，天哪，托比和安吉拉居然很高兴看到迈克尔和奥斯卡。

1281
00:57:36.520 --> 00:57:36.940
Yeah.
是啊。

1282
00:57:37.360 --> 00:57:43.060
Like I expect Pam to smile at him, you know, but the fact that Toby and Angela were relieved
帕姆对他笑我能理解，但托比和安吉拉看到迈克尔时居然如释重负，

1283
00:57:43.060 --> 00:57:43.920
to see Michael.
这让我很意外。

1284
00:57:44.180 --> 00:57:47.080
Well, they did not enjoy Jim being in charge.
毕竟他们不喜欢吉姆当负责人。

1285
00:57:47.420 --> 00:57:47.840
No.
没错。

1286
00:57:47.840 --> 00:57:50.880
We had a fan catch in this scene, Angela.
安吉拉，这一幕里有粉丝发现了一个细节。

1287
00:57:51.160 --> 00:57:51.420
Okay.
好的。

1288
00:57:51.780 --> 00:57:58.540
From Andrea T., who would like to know who made the peach cobbler for Creed?
来自安德里亚·T的提问，她想知道是谁给克里德做的桃子脆皮馅饼？

1289
00:57:58.880 --> 00:58:01.260
Because it's in a Pyrex dish.
因为它装在百利耐热玻璃盘里。

1290
00:58:01.400 --> 00:58:02.600
It's clearly homemade.
显然是自制的。

1291
00:58:02.920 --> 00:58:08.840
Did Angela go home and make this cobbler because she is so dedicated to throwing the perfect birthday
安吉拉是不是专门回家做了这个馅饼，因为她致力于举办一场完美的生日

1292
00:58:08.840 --> 00:58:09.220
party?
派对？

1293
00:58:09.460 --> 00:58:11.720
So listen, I thought about this too.
听着，我也想过这个问题。

1294
00:58:11.720 --> 00:58:14.180
And I think Angela did.
我觉得就是安吉拉做的。

1295
00:58:14.180 --> 00:58:19.620
I think when Creed said to Jim, tell Angela it's for Creed, she'll know what to do.
我想当克里德对吉姆说“告诉安吉拉这是给克里德的，她会知道该怎么做”时，

1296
00:58:19.840 --> 00:58:22.940
Angela went home and made his favorite peach cobbler pie.
安吉拉就回家做了他最爱的桃子脆皮馅饼。

1297
00:58:23.300 --> 00:58:24.280
I'm impressed.
我被折服了。

1298
00:58:24.760 --> 00:58:25.020
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1299
00:58:25.400 --> 00:58:30.620
Well, at 18 minutes, 56 seconds, you guys, there is a great shot of the Fudgie the Whale
对了，在18分56秒，大家注意看，有一个关于“鲸鱼福吉”

1300
00:58:30.620 --> 00:58:30.920
cake.
蛋糕的绝佳镜头。

1301
00:58:30.920 --> 00:58:32.500
Oh, so there you go.
噢，原来是这样。

1302
00:58:32.500 --> 00:58:33.100
It was there.
它就在那儿。

1303
00:58:33.240 --> 00:58:33.940
Proof of Fudgie.
法吉存在的证据。

1304
00:58:34.180 --> 00:58:35.260
Proof of Fudgie.
法吉存在的证据。

1305
00:58:35.680 --> 00:58:42.480
And Jenna, as we're wrapping up this scene, Jim and Michael have this fantastic moment where
珍娜，在我们结束这一幕时，吉姆和迈克尔有段精彩的对话，当时

1306
00:58:42.480 --> 00:58:45.800
Jim is like, I tried to do all of their parties on one day.
吉姆说，我试着把他们所有的生日派对都安排在同一天。

1307
00:58:45.960 --> 00:58:48.100
And Michael's like, oh, yeah, I did that.
迈克尔就说，噢，是啊，我以前也干过。

1308
00:58:48.380 --> 00:58:48.560
Yeah.
是啊。

1309
00:58:48.680 --> 00:58:49.440
Rookie mistake.
新手常犯的错。

1310
00:58:49.780 --> 00:58:50.820
You'll figure it out.
你会慢慢摸索出来的。

1311
00:58:51.180 --> 00:58:53.400
This scene is so beautiful.
这一幕太美好了。

1312
00:58:53.940 --> 00:59:00.800
It's this glimpse into Michael where he's kind of talking to a peer, right?
这让我们瞥见了迈克尔人性的一面，他当时是在和同僚对话，对吧？

1313
00:59:00.920 --> 00:59:06.320
He's always managering us or always wanting to be in that position of status to us.
他平时总是在管理我们，或者总是想在我们面前保持那种地位。

1314
00:59:06.400 --> 00:59:10.040
But here he is talking manager on manager to Jim.
但在这里，他是在以经理对经理的身份和吉姆交谈。

1315
00:59:10.540 --> 00:59:11.520
It's amazing.
太棒了。

1316
00:59:11.940 --> 00:59:13.000
It's so great.
真是太好了。

1317
00:59:13.020 --> 00:59:14.860
And it's such a human moment.
这真是个充满人情味的时刻。

1318
00:59:15.080 --> 00:59:17.080
You know, Jim's like, I'm not going to be here in 10 years.
你知道，吉姆说，我十年后可不会待在这儿了。

1319
00:59:17.200 --> 00:59:18.620
And Michael's like, yeah, that's what I said.
迈克尔就说，是啊，我当年也是这么说的。

1320
00:59:18.620 --> 00:59:24.720
So as we close out this episode, Jenna, I thought we could hear just the final end of Jim and
所以在本集结束之际，珍娜，我想我们可以听听吉姆和

1321
00:59:24.720 --> 00:59:25.680
Michael's scene together.
迈克尔对手戏的最后部分。

1322
00:59:25.940 --> 00:59:26.860
Sam, can you play that?
萨姆，能放一下吗？

1323
00:59:28.950 --> 00:59:29.870
Sure glad you're back.
真高兴你回来了。

1324
00:59:30.710 --> 00:59:31.890
You are relieved.
你如释重负啊。

1325
00:59:32.390 --> 00:59:33.510
You have no idea.
你根本无法想象。

1326
00:59:34.910 --> 00:59:35.730
So what did I miss?
那我错过了什么？

1327
00:59:36.610 --> 00:59:39.050
Well, I tried to put all the birthdays together at once.
嗯，我试着把所有人的生日聚在一起过。

1328
00:59:39.250 --> 00:59:39.470
Oh.
噢。

1329
00:59:39.670 --> 00:59:40.970
So terrible idea.
真是个糟糕的主意。

1330
00:59:41.190 --> 00:59:41.350
Yeah.
是啊。

1331
00:59:41.650 --> 00:59:41.910
Okay.
好吧。

1332
00:59:42.170 --> 00:59:42.810
I did that.
我以前也干过。

1333
00:59:43.710 --> 00:59:44.550
Rookie mistake.
新手常犯的错。

1334
00:59:44.890 --> 00:59:45.650
You did do it?
你真的干过？

1335
00:59:45.750 --> 00:59:46.070
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1336
00:59:46.410 --> 00:59:49.370
Now, let's wait 10 years.
现在，让我们等上十年。

1337
00:59:49.370 --> 00:59:50.370
You'll figure it out.
你会慢慢摸索出来的。

1338
00:59:51.030 --> 00:59:53.230
Well, I don't think I'll be here in 10 years.
嗯，我觉得我十年后不会待在这儿了。

1339
00:59:55.070 --> 00:59:55.990
That's what I said.
我当年也是这么说的。

1340
01:00:01.440 --> 01:00:02.200
That's what she said.
那是她说的。

1341
01:00:06.140 --> 01:00:07.020
That's what who said?
那是谁说的？

1342
01:00:07.540 --> 01:00:08.500
I never know.
我从来都不知道。

1343
01:00:10.100 --> 01:00:11.220
I just say it.
我只是随口一说。

1344
01:00:12.500 --> 01:00:18.240
I say stuff like that, you know, to lighten the tension when things sort of get hard.
我会说那种话，你知道的，是为了在气氛变得沉重时缓解一下紧张感。

1345
01:00:18.520 --> 01:00:19.320
That's what she said.
那是她说的。

1346
01:00:20.680 --> 01:00:21.160
Hey.
嘿。

1347
01:00:22.120 --> 01:00:22.600
Nice.
不错。

1348
01:00:24.320 --> 01:00:25.140
Really good.
非常好。

1349
01:00:27.940 --> 01:00:28.420
Bravo.
太棒了。

1350
01:00:29.640 --> 01:00:30.580
My young ward.
我的年轻门徒。

1351
01:00:33.450 --> 01:00:34.570
I have a question.
我有一个问题。

1352
01:00:35.050 --> 01:00:35.350
Yeah.
嗯。

1353
01:00:35.670 --> 01:00:38.730
Is Michael finally eating what was in the bag?
迈克尔终于在吃袋子里的东西了吗？

1354
01:00:40.110 --> 01:00:42.230
It sounds like he's eating nuts.
听起来像是在吃坚果。

1355
01:00:42.790 --> 01:00:43.430
Yeah.
是啊。

1356
01:00:43.430 --> 01:00:47.770
I looked at it and it's like, I can't tell what they are.
我看了看，怎么说呢，我看不出那是什么。

1357
01:00:47.990 --> 01:00:49.590
Little pretzel bites.
小块的椒盐脆饼。

1358
01:00:49.970 --> 01:00:51.430
You know what they look like?
你知道它们看起来像什么吗？

1359
01:00:51.430 --> 01:00:56.950
If you get a Chex mix, there are these little stubby pretzel bite things.
如果你买过切克斯混合零食，里面会有那种短短的椒盐脆饼块。

1360
01:00:57.250 --> 01:00:57.590
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1361
01:00:57.830 --> 01:00:58.830
I don't know.
我不知道。

1362
01:00:58.970 --> 01:01:00.630
Or they look like slivered almonds.
或者看起来像杏仁片。

1363
01:01:01.030 --> 01:01:02.010
Or pecans.
或者是山核桃。

1364
01:01:02.350 --> 01:01:03.690
It's such a mystery.
真是个谜。

1365
01:01:04.310 --> 01:01:12.030
But as I watched that lovely scene that I absolutely love, I was wondering, what is he eating?
但在我观看那个我非常喜欢的精彩片段时，我一直在想，他到底在吃什么？

1366
01:01:13.790 --> 01:01:15.450
I'd forgotten about it.
我都快忘了这事了。

1367
01:01:15.870 --> 01:01:17.550
I'll have to go back and look.
我得回去再看看。

1368
01:01:18.230 --> 01:01:18.450
Ah.
啊。

1369
01:01:18.930 --> 01:01:22.030
Well, you guys, that was Survivorman.
好了，各位，刚才那是《求生者》。

1370
01:01:22.470 --> 01:01:24.510
I don't think I'd make it out in the woods.
我觉得我没法在野外生存。

1371
01:01:24.510 --> 01:01:26.770
I do think I'd make it at party planning.
但我确实觉得我能胜任派对策划。

1372
01:01:27.050 --> 01:01:29.190
I'd make sure everyone had their dang cake.
我会确保每个人都能吃到该死的蛋糕。

1373
01:01:30.130 --> 01:01:37.570
Next week, we have the deposition that has some of my favorite scenes of all time.
下周，我们将讨论那场证词陈述，里面有一些我个人最喜欢的场景。

1374
01:01:38.410 --> 01:01:38.770
Brilliant.
太棒了。

1375
01:01:39.310 --> 01:01:40.710
Thank you so much for listening.
非常感谢大家的收听。

1376
01:01:40.870 --> 01:01:43.370
Thank you for sending in your questions and your comments.
感谢大家发来的问题和评论。

1377
01:01:43.370 --> 01:01:44.330
We love it.
我们很喜欢。

1378
01:01:44.430 --> 01:01:45.490
We love you guys.
我们爱你们。

1379
01:01:46.070 --> 01:01:48.910
Everyone send Angela a cake on her birthday.
大家记得在安吉拉生日时给她寄蛋糕。

1380
01:01:49.330 --> 01:01:50.230
No, no, no, no.
不，不，不，不。

1381
01:01:51.070 --> 01:01:52.310
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1382
01:01:52.830 --> 01:01:53.330
All right.
好吧。

1383
01:01:53.430 --> 01:01:53.910
Bye, guys.
再见，各位。

1384
01:01:54.170 --> 01:01:54.570
Bye.
再见。

